{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 2, :comments ["<b>Speak to Aaron.</b> This commandment is juxtaposed after the dedication of the princes, because you find that twelve tribes offered their offering for the dedication of the altar, and the tribe of Levi did not offer. That is to say, they were distressed and said: why were we kept far from offering for the dedication of the altar to the Holy One, blessed be He? Once the dedication of the altar had passed, the Holy One, blessed be He, said to Aaron and his sons: all the tribes made a dedication, and you — you shall make a dedication of your own. Therefore it says: speak to Aaron, 'When you mount' etc., and afterward: take the Levites." "<b>When you mount the lamps.</b> It was stated on the day the Tabernacle was erected, because on that day they began to kindle them. After he finished erecting the Tabernacle, he needed to be commanded about the kindling of the Menorah — to teach you that even at night the divine speech occurred, for there the lamp is always burning. And so we find in Samuel: 'and the lamp of Elohim had not yet gone out' etc., and 'YHWH called to Samuel.' <b>When you mount the lamps toward the face of the Menorah.</b> At the time of their kindling, you stand opposite the face of the Menorah and kindle — then <b>the seven lamps shall give light.</b> And 'toward the face of the Menorah' is not to be connected to 'the seven lamps shall give light,' and proof is from the verse after it: 'toward the face of the Menorah he mounted its lamps.' Another interpretation: <b>When you mount the lamps</b> — as its plain meaning, the language of going up: when you bring up the lamps onto the branches to their place, and do not say they were fixed on them, for it is written in the portion of ויקהל: 'and he made the Menorah' etc. 'and he made its lamps seven, and its tongs' etc. <b>Toward the face of the Menorah the seven lamps shall give light.</b> He arranged the openings of the seven lamps toward the face of the Menorah, that is, the parokhet that separates between the Hekhal and the Holy of Holies. And that is according to the one who says they were placed north and south; but according to the one who says they were placed east and west, <b>toward the face of the Menorah</b> — that is, the table, as it is written in the portion of פקודי: 'and he placed the Menorah opposite the table.'" "<b>The seven lamps shall give light.</b> The lamps on the six branches — thus is the version in Rashi's commentary, except that the scribes removed one word from it."], :book :numbers, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 8, :notes {2 "ה״ג = 'this is the version/girsa'; פרש״‎י = the commentary of Rashi. The 'one word' removed refers to a textual variant in Rashi's comment on this verse."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:16:59.537713464Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}